  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of the plane through (1,2,-3) and (2,-2,1) and parallel to $X$ -axis is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EolJL",
      "text": "$y-z+1=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9OnI6",
      "text": "$y-z-1=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SDiBT",
      "text": "$y+z-1=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "InkQd",
      "text": "$y+z+1=0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation of the plane will be $\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}x-1 & y-2 & z+3 \\\\ 2-1 & -2-2 & 1-(-3) \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right|=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}x-1 & y-2 & z+3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right|=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 1[4(y-2)+4(z+3)]=0$\r\n[Expanding along $\\left.R_{j}\\right]$ \r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 4 y-8+4 z+12=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 4 y+4 z+4=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad y+z+1=0$",
    "image": null
  },
